    "modification": "Removed three automatic fsck_hfs commands from restored_external, retaining partition readiness checks, USB initialization, kernel boot arguments and original read-only data mounting. Added a strict decimal --sleep SECONDS mode (0..3600) which returns before hardware initialization and resumes interrupted libc sleep calls. Require an HFS /dev/md0 root; skip an already writable root, otherwise use a checked mount(2) update with the pinned XNU HFS arguments to avoid mount_hfs reopening the mounted RAM device.",
